# ─── EmailJS Configuration (contact form) ──────────────────────────────────
# Sign up at https://dashboard.emailjs.com/ and copy these values into a new
# file called `.env` (this `.env.example` is committed as documentation only).
#
# Once configured, the contact form on the homepage sends emails directly to
# your inbox without any backend. Until you fill these in, the form gracefully
# falls back to opening the visitor's email client via mailto:.

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=

# ─── AI Chatbot (works with ZERO configuration) ────────────────────────────
# The chatbot calls POST /api/chat — a Vercel Serverless Function grounded in
# src/data/factSheet.js. Provider chain:
#   1. GLM_API_KEY set      → Z.ai open platform (glm-4.5-flash, free tier)
#   2. No key (default)     → Pollinations keyless endpoint (free, real model)
#   3. Both fail            → built-in rule-based engine, so it never breaks
#
# OPTIONAL: for GLM-branded answers, create a free key at https://z.ai
# (API Keys) and add it in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables:
GLM_API_KEY=
